### Quest Lines ###

## GT Steam Reborn

betterquesting.questline.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lGT Steam Reborn
betterquesting.questline.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=A full steam-age expansion for GregTech: 23 steam multiblocks, the singularity tech chain, and a cross-dimensional hub-and-node logistics network.%n%nSix chapters: steam economics, three wells of steam, the processing matrix, hub logistics, singularity graduation, and endgame conveniences.%n%nSteam is all you need.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§2§lSteam! Steam! Steam!
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=Welcome to the final shape of steam. GTSR bolts §623 steam multiblock controllers§r, a §dsingularity tech chain§r and a cross-dimensional hub-and-node logistics network onto GregTech.%n%nSix chapters lie ahead: §6steam economics§r, §6three wells of steam§r, §3the processing matrix§r, §5hub logistics§r, §dsingularity graduation§r and §3endgame conveniences§r.%n%nEvery machine is taught in two tracks — a mechanics lesson first, then a hands-on acceptance where you craft the controller and show it to the book.%n%n§8§oZero EU needed to graduate.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.name=§6§lSteam Economics
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.desc=Every machine in the steam age eventually settles its bill on one formula. Memorize it — it pays better than any recipe.%n%nThe master formula: §6steam per tick = (−lEUt × 10000) ÷ max(1000, efficiency)§r, in §6L/tick§r — §1multiply by 20 to get L/s§r. Never mix the two units again.%n%nOnly recipes with lEUt < 0 are billed, and the efficiency in the denominator is a global multiplier — the next quest is exactly its trap.%n%n§3§nLearn the formula before you light the machines.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.name=§6§lThe Efficiency Trap
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.desc=Efficiency is the bill's hidden lever: at §15000§r the steam §1halves§r; halve the efficiency and the bill doubles.%n%nThe real trap is the floor: §1max(1000, …)§r clamps the worst case at §1ten-fold§r. The moment a steel VSP slides below §11000§r, §6200 L/t§r balloons into §62,000 L/t = 40,000 L/s§r — no boiler fills that hole.%n%nOnce the spiral starts, the line only sinks deeper, until it stops outright.%n%n§cWatch the efficiency, watch your lifeline.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.name=§6§lSuperheated Means 4x
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.desc=Superheated steam is not “better steam” — it is another tempo: the machine draws §14x steam§r per tick while recipe duration goes §1÷4§r, a net §1four-fold speedup§r.%n%nThe comforting part: total steam per recipe §2stays unchanged§r; only the pacing of throughput moves, so your capacity planning survives.%n%nBronze included, no tier gate — the earlier you switch, the earlier you enjoy it.%n%n§3Want throughput? Make superheated first.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.name=§6§lThe Cooling Ledger
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.desc=Where does spent steam go? This ledger is worth auditing line by line. Plain steam condenses at §1160L to 1L§r distilled water into the normal cooling hatch; superheated steam degrades §11:1§r back into plain steam and lands in the pressure cooling hatch.%n%nNothing is lost without a hatch either — leftovers pend until one is fitted (since v1.10.61).%n%nReturn that distilled water to the boiler, and scale stops being your problem.%n%n§2Distilled water back to the boiler, no more scale headaches.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.name=§6§lFit the Cooling Hatches
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.desc=Put the ledger into hardware: the normal cooling hatch holds §664,000L§r and outputs §63,200 L/t§r; the pressure cooling hatch holds §61,024,000L§r at §651,200 L/t§r.%n%nThis quest has you craft one of each and verify the return-flow books by hand.%n%nThey are the standard water-return ports on every steam multiblock — skimp on them and the ledger stops balancing.%n%n§3No water on the floor, no steam wasted.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.name=§6§lThe Free 4x Loop
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.desc=String chapter A's formulas into one closed production line: the compressor drinks §66,400 steam/s§r, puts out §61,600 superheated/s§r and tips §130 L/s§r of distilled water back; that water reboils into §64,800 steam/s§r.%n%nOn this loop a bronze air compressor rated §6400 L/s§r runs on superheated as §63,200 L air/s§r — §2a 4x throughput at zero net steam cost§r.%n%nLine up the reservoir, the compressor and the steam eaters in a row, and the books close themselves.%n%n§8§oSteam burns, and the accounts balance themselves.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.name=§6§lThree Wells of Steam
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.desc=Boilers were never the only well — GTSR digs three new ones: the §6geothermal boiler§r burns magma (§660k/150k L/s§r), the §6solar array§r drinks sunshine (§6120k/180k/240k L/s§r), and the §6gear compressor§r squeezes plain steam §14:1§r into superheated.%n%nEach has a temperament: geothermal wants magma plumbing, solar lives on the weather, the compressor eats total volume.%n%nWalk each branch once, then meet again at the selection review.%n%n§3Sun by day, magma by night, compressor whenever superheated runs short.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.name=§6§lGeothermal: Burn the Magma
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.desc=The geothermal boiler is the most direct idea of all: burn magma as fuel. A hot bronze unit turns §6375 water/s§r into §660,000 L/s§r; steel takes §6937 water/s§r yet yields only §6149,920 L/s§r — integer division, not a clean 150,000.%n%nThe magma side has its own meter: §6333 mB/s§r on a cold machine, §6200§r on hot steel, §6250 mB/s§r once the overheat chip is in.%n%nByproducts roll on a probability table from §120% obsidian§r down to §10.35% gold§r — lucky rolls are pure profit.%n%n§8§oBurn the planet's core, mine the planet's purse.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.name=§6§lScale and Overpressure
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.desc=Scale never zeroes output: at full scale the yield is §1max(1%, 1−0.99×scale)§r — a §11%§r floor, not zero, but nothing to look at either.%n%nThe clock: full scale takes §112 hours§r on bronze, §14h§r on steel, §12h§r with the chip. Overpressure mode caps heat at §12.0§r; plain water skipping the §11-hour§r delay gains §1+0.2§r per step, crushing §112 hours§r into §136 minutes§r.%n%nPush heat to §1200%§r and output §1doubles§r — even bronze hits §6120,000 L/s§r.%n%n§cScale is a time tax; compute the rate before you pay.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.name=§6§lLight the Geothermal Boiler
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.desc=Acceptance time: craft the Large Geothermal Boiler controller yourself and show it to the book — display-only, nothing is taken.%n%nStructure-wise, match the §3casing, pipe, gearbox and frame§r in one tier, hook a magma pump and a steady water source, and a §660,000 L/s§r bronze steam well is online.%n%nWith the overheat chip fitted it moonlights as a superheated producer — two machines in one.%n%n§2One geothermal well, steam around the clock.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.name=§6§lSteam from the Sun
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.desc=The solar array moves the boiler room into the sky, in three tiers: §6120,000 / 180,000 / 240,000 L/s§r — and the nickel tier emits superheated directly.%n%nBoosters are the bonus engine: heat gain adds up to §1+200%§r, capped at §1×3.0§r; the total multiplier adds as §1solar + heat − 1§r, so the bonuses never trample each other.%n%nThe §6960,000 L/s superheated§r peak demands noon, clear sky, no scale and full water — all four.%n%n§cFor nights and rain, keep a reservoir.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.name=§6§lRoll Out the Solar Array
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Large Solar Oven Array controller (display-only).%n%nTiers rise with the multiblock's size — bronze, steel, nickel — and the nickel tier emits superheated outright; casing, pipe, gearbox and frame must match the tier to form.%n%nThe booster and heat-gain arithmetic was already done in the mechanics lesson.%n%n§2Move the boiler room into the sky — the sun is your fuel depot.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.name=§6§lThe Four-to-One Gate
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.desc=The Gear Steam Compressor is the master gate of superheated: bronze takes §66,400 steam/s§r into §61,600 superheated/s§r and returns §130 L/s§r distilled; steel does §625,600 into 6,400§r with §1120§r back.%n%nStructural discipline as always: casing, pipe, gearbox and frame must form in the §3same tier§r.%n%nConservation written plainly: §64,800 + 1,600 = 6,400§r — the condensate closes the loop.%n%n§3One compressor, and the whole base knows where its superheated comes from.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.name=§6§lCompressor Online
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Gear Steam Compressor controller (display-only).%n%nIt is the §3master gate§r of superheated for the whole base: bronze starts at §61,600 superheated/s§r, steel §1quadruples§r it to §66,400§r — and it neither cares about weather nor geology.%n%nThe returned distilled water goes straight back to the boilers, nearly balancing the books — a free grade upgrade.%n%n§2With it on duty, the furnace and the endgame machines fire at will.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.name=§6§lChoose Your Wells
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.desc=The three wells meet — selection time: geothermal eats §3capital cost§r in exchange for round-the-clock output, but wants magma plumbing; solar runs §1full by day, zero by night§r and must shave its peaks with reservoirs; the compressor converts §1steam surplus§r into superheated — the most flexible, and the hungriest for total volume.%n%nThere is no standard answer, only fit or misfit — ratio them by your base's §3veins, weather and steam ledger§r.%n%n§8§oAdults, of course, take all three.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.name=§3§lThe Bronze Matrix
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.desc=Chapter C opens with the workhorses: §3the Large Steam Furnace, Air Compressor, Atmospheric Centrifuge, Fluid Drill, Pyrolyzer, the three kiln brothers, the Siemens-Martin and the Ammonia Plant§r, plus the borer and the chip sidelines.%n%nMany machines, one accountant: every drop of steam still bills through chapter A's master formula — §6L/s§r pricing, efficiency denominator and all.%n%nEach machine keeps the same rhythm: mechanics lesson first, acceptance second.%n%n§3The more machines you run, the better you must count.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.name=§3§lThe Big Steam Furnace
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.desc=The Large Steam Furnace is the bronze base's smelting workhorse — one machine for a whole row of single furnaces. It re-prices “8 EU/t smelting” into a steam bill, and the whole story is parallelism and discounts.%n%nBronze runs §124 parallels, 0.6 EUt discount, duration ÷2.5§r — about §6115.2 L/t ≈ 2,300 L/s§r; steel §148 parallels, 0.4, ÷5§r — §6153.6 L/t ≈ 3,072 L/s§r.%n%n§cTrust no old manual's “48,000 L/s” — that is the 20.8-fold accident of reading L/t as L/s; redo the math and the ledger turns clean.§r%n%n§8§oNumbers speak, but only in the right units.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.name=§3§lFurnace, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Large Steam Furnace controller (display-only).%n%nEven the bronze tier smelts at §12,300 L/s§r-class throughput with §124-way parallelism§r on a single steam main; casing, pipe, gearbox and frame form in one tier.%n%nThe steel upgrade doubles and discounts again — no re-plumbing required.%n%n§2One furnace line feeds a whole bronze base.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.name=§3§lWhere Air Comes From
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.desc=Air does not come from nowhere — and the Air Compressor checks no recipes: it pumps on a beat, every §120 ticks§r putting out §1800 × parallels§r liters of air, blunt and honest.%n%nA bronze cycle trades §6400 L steam§r for §6800 L air§r; steel with §14 parallels§r does §61,200 → 3,200§r — four times the scale.%n%nWhen tank pressure runs low it switches to the lower air tier automatically — §3the line never stalls§r.%n%n§8§oThe wind is free; the pump is not.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.name=§3§lAir Compressor, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Large Air Compressor controller (display-only).%n%nIt upgrades §6air supply§r from a pump workshop to an industrial main — the centrifuge, the Siemens-Martin and the ammonia plant all queue downstream for gas.%n%nThe steel form's §63,200 L air/s§r is the ticket to a fully fed furnace, and the foundation of the chemical chain.%n%n§2When the blowers spin, the money rolls in.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.name=§3§lCentrifuge the Sky
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.desc=The Atmospheric Centrifuge runs §14 / 16§r parallels (bronze/steel) and takes air apart into its components — the gateway of the chemical chain.%n%nThe Rare Gas Separation Chip is a §3recipe-table switch§r, not an accelerator: steel-only; once fitted, only recipes with §1more than 3 fluid outputs§r run, while the common recipes lock out.%n%nA chip is not a master key — fitted to the wrong tier it is pure waste.%n%n§cA chip on a bronze unit does nothing. Don't waste it.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.name=§3§lThe Rare Gas Gate
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Atmospheric Centrifuge controller plus a Rare Gas Separation Chip (display-only).%n%nSteel plus chip is what actually opens the door to §3krypton, xenon, neon and helium§r — the first sip of glow components and the deeper tech beyond.%n%nOnce more, because it bears repeating: the chip only works on steel. On a bronze unit it is an expensive souvenir.%n%n§2Rare-gas independence starts here.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.name=§3§lDrilling 101
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.desc=Settle the Steam Fluid Drill's oil ledger before you dig: bronze climbs from §1200 L/s§r to §12,000 L/s§r; steel starts the same but reaches §18,000 L/s§r — base cost §61,000 L/s§r steam, cycle §120 ticks§r.%n%nStructural discipline is strict: exactly §11§r steam input hatch — bring two and the shape refuses to form.%n%nSurvey the field before raising the derrick, and lay the tanks before the oil arrives; the order matters.%n%n§3One good well, half an oil field.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.name=§3§lFour Modes, One Climb
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.desc=Drill efficiency climbs in §1points§r, not percentages: bronze gains §1+33 per cycle§r — about §1303 cycles ≈ 5 minutes§r to full; steel gains only §1+3§r, a grind of roughly §156 minutes§r.%n%nThe four modes each yield differently: §1water 100%, distilled 20%, brine 10%, magma 0.5%§r (floor 5%); brine and magma modes cost §64,000 L/s§r.%n%nMode switching is steel-only, and switching §cresets the efficiency§r — decide before you touch it.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.name=§3§lThe Drill, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Steam Fluid Drill controller (display-only).%n%nOnce more on the §6two-input ban§r: exactly one steam input hatch, not one more; the same-tier casing rule applies as ever.%n%nAt full efficiency a steel well's §18,000 L/s§r of crude feeds an entire pyrolysis-and-refining chain.%n%n§2One steel well, eight thousand liters — the tank farm never runs dry.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.name=§3§lPyrolyze the Vein
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.desc=The Vein Steam Pyrolyzer sits right on the oil vein and cracks it in place: lEUt §1−50/−200§r becomes §61,000/4,000 L/s§r at full efficiency, cycles of §1360/180 s§r.%n%nIts finest virtue is backfill: every cycle returns §1+10,000 / +25,000 mB§r to the chunk — mining without draining the ledger, the vein steadier the longer you work it.%n%nRange chips cover §12×2 / 4×4 / 8×8§r; T1→T3 absorb the tier below, and the voltage gate walks HV→IV.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.name=§3§lPyrolyzer, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Vein Steam Pyrolyzer controller and its §3T1 range chip§r (display-only).%n%nThe moment the chip goes in, the oil of a §12×2-chunk§r field answers to it; T2 and T3 absorb the tier below — no sunk costs.%n%nBackfill keeps the vein stable while the drill feeds it from the other side — supply without end.%n%n§2The oil field becomes a printing press.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.name=§3§lThree Kiln Brothers
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.desc=The kiln district assembles its three brothers: the Reinforced Brick Blast Furnace, the Large Coke Oven and the Crust Steam Borer.%n%nThe blast furnace's heat ledger is the delicate one: §1+0.01%/s§r running, §1−1%/s§r idle, speed §1×(1+0.5×heat)§r up to §11.5x§r, parallelism §11→4§r; the coke oven shifts §10.0001/0.001 per s§r, §124/64§r parallels, base speed §1×1.2/×2.0§r.%n%nThe borer drinks §62,000 L/s§r per §1500-tick§r cycle — §1quadruple speed on superheated: 125 ticks§r — rolling ores from a void-drop table.%n%n§8§oFire all three and the neighbors think you brew elixirs.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.name=§3§lThe Kilns, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.desc=Acceptance: hand in all three brothers at once — the controllers of the blast furnace, the coke oven and the crust borer (display-only).%n%nThree lines put out §3steel, coke and ores§r; leave three spare branches on the steam main for them.%n%nThe borer's void-drop table occasionally surprises — put a hopper underneath.%n%n§2Kiln district lit: the bronze base is properly industrial now.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.name=§3§lA Furnace Fed by Fire
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.desc=The Siemens-Martin is picky by birth: §csuperheated steam only§r — plain steam cannot even get in the door. Preheat draws §6300 L/t (6,000 L/s)§r; past §1100%§r heat it settles to §6150 L/t§r, and at §1200%§r just §675 L/t§r. It also demands §61,000 L/s§r of air.%n%nPast §1100%§r, heat climbs §1+0.01% per second§r; every §11%§r shaves §10.5%§r off recipe time, capped at §1half§r; parallelism scales §164→128§r.%n%n§3Chapter B's master gate was built for exactly this machine.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.name=§3§lSiemens-Martin, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Siemens-Martin Furnace controller (display-only).%n%nBefore ignition, confirm both the §6superheated main§r and the §6air main§r reach its door: missing either, it never survives the preheat.%n%n§164-parallel§r-class smelting throughput is the real gate of the steel age.%n%n§2The day the furnace runs full is the day steel is measured in tons.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.name=§3§lAmmonia and Seven Catalysts
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.desc=The Ammonia Plant is chapter C's chemistry finale: preheat takes §68,000 steam/s§r plus §6200 refinery gas/s§r, running costs §612,000 + 200§r.%n%nExtra steam follows a formula: §1parallel × 16,000 ÷ reaction seconds§r — the quantum tier at §1256 parallels§r demands §64,096,000 L/s§r, the fiercest single-machine steam bill in the pack.%n%nSeven catalysts unlock seven routes, and the plant even tips superheated steam back as a gift.%n%n§dThis line is already pouring the quantum age's foundation.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.name=§5§lHub Logistics
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.desc=The hub-logistics era begins, and one rule outranks all: a hub §cwithout a chip only stores§r — fit a §dhub singularity chip§r and transfer actually starts.%n%nFrom then on, every §120 ticks§r a round batch-moves the bound nodes' throughput; §3cross-chunk and cross-dimension are each just one binding§r.%n%nEither prerequisite works: finish the processing matrix properly, or arrive rich in steam.%n%n§8§oFrom today, pipes are decoration.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.name=§5§lTwo Reservoirs
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.desc=The hub reservoirs hold astronomical numbers — unreal-looking, but every one sourced: pressure cells §63.2 billion L§r, reinforced §612.8§r, overpressure §6204.8 billion§r; hub singularity chips ×5, reinforced ×20 — and the §1×20§r wins.%n%nStructurally each stack layer holds §125 cells × 30 layers = 750§r; auto-output runs §61,000,000 L/tick§r — yes, twenty million L/s.%n%nThe water side stores §11.28M/5.12M/20.48M L§r at §664,000 L/t§r; overflow mode demands §1≥90%§r fill; overflow is automatic, the storage banked by hand.%n%n§8§oThis is not a reservoir. This is a sea.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.name=§5§lThe Hubs, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.desc=Acceptance: hand in both reservoirs at once — the steam hub accumulator and the water hub accumulator (display-only).%n%nSHA-side auto-output of §61,000,000 L/tick§r means downstream machines never see the word “thirsty” again; the WHA side dispatches all the base's condensate from one common bank.%n%nAnd do chip both: §cwithout chips they only store§r.%n%n§2Reservoirs up — the base's steam heartbeat is steady.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.name=§5§lSix Cache Nodes
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.desc=Nodes are the logistics network's capillaries — choosing right beats piling more. The six, capacity/rate: steam §616M/2M§r, reinforced §664M/8M§r, overpressure §6256M/64M§r, generic fluid §62M/64k§r, reinforced fluid §68M/256k§r, overpressure fluid §632M/2M L/s§r.%n%nRates come in §110 steps§r, tunable to each downstream's appetite; the singularity cost of binding: reinforced steam §d1§r, overpressure steam a §dlevel-3 hub plus a reinforced chip§r, the rest of the family §d0§r.%n%n§3Small nodes, big shoes, spread like stars.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.name=§5§lThe 600-Tick Rebind
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.desc=The node heartbeat is written straight into the source: §1mNextRegistrationTick = aTick + (registered ? 600 : 20)§r.%n%nTranslated: after a successful registration, an idempotent recheck every §1600 ticks (30 s)§r confirms the binding holds; on failure, a retry every §120 ticks§r — it never gives up.%n%nThe registration itself carries §3cross-dimensional chunk loading§r, so remote nodes take effect at once.%n%n§cBreaking a node refunds no singularity — the consumption marker stays, no freeloading.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.name=§5§lThe Nodes, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.desc=Acceptance: hand in the steam cache node and the generic fluid cache node (display-only) — two ambassadors of the §dzero-singularity§r family.%n%nNot one singularity spent, and §616M L§r of steam and §62M L§r of fluid buffering reach a thousand blocks away.%n%n§110 rate steps§r tune to each downstream's appetite — supply what is missing, wherever it is missing, and expand for free.%n%n§2Logistics freedom starts at zero cost.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.name=§5§lFour Singularity Compartments
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.desc=Hand in all four singularity compartments at once (display-only): the steam pair moves §68,000,000 L/s§r, the fluid pair §6256,000 L/s§r; capacity numerically equals the rate, and direction is locked against backflow.%n%nThey are the hub network's §dhigh-throughput gates§r: place one at each end of a line, one swallowing, one emitting.%n%nNothing pipes the middle — distance and dimensions are no longer arguments.%n%n§2With billion-grade throughput, the pipe age retires.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.name=§5§lTerminals and Hub Chips
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.desc=The Hub Terminal is a remote control for your pocket: hold it to §1teleport at 1 singularity per 8 blocks§r; hub chip multipliers §1×5§r, reinforced §1×20§r.%n%nThe reinforced hub singularity chip's bill is the one recipe in this whole line worth copying down — read it item by item: a base of §d384 singularities§r (6×64), plus §116 UV circuits§r, §132 dense europium plates§r and §164 dense rhodium-palladium plates§r, soaked in §6radon 128,000 mB§r, then §1960 s§r on a §1LuV§r assembler.%n%n§cThis is not crafting. This is a mortgage.§r%n%n§8§oInstallment plan — and the singularities don't stay.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.name=§5§lFull-Network Check
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.desc=Chapter close: put the §3chip–node–terminal§r three layers each in place, and the full-network check begins.%n%nChips in the hubs, nodes bound to the hubs, terminal in hand; when a §1600-tick§r batch round flows and the cache nodes start breathing, this logistics network counts as alive.%n%nAll four acceptance pieces are already on you — the perfect moment to wire everything together.%n%n§8§oThe moment the logistics graph connects beats any boss fight.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.name=§d§lSingularity Graduation
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.desc=Graduation opens: the §dsingularity§r becomes hard currency. Chain overview — the entangler mass-produces singularities, the DSM presses them §11000:1§r into dense, the CSC presses those into critical, and the SDH's twin nodes burn them for work.%n%nFrom this chapter on, every bill is priced in §dunits§r — steam itself becomes the small change.%n%nSteam-rich players may walk straight in from chapter A's closed loop, without finishing C and D.%n%n§3The steam age ends with steam itself collapsing.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.name=§d§lA Wild Singularity
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.desc=Wild singularities generate only in the §3Overworld and the Nether§r, roughly one per §148×48 chunks§r — finding them is pure legwork and luck.%n%nThe threshold is mercifully low: hardness §14§r, punchable by hand, dropping §10-1§r. But a dropped plain singularity detonates after §1100 ticks (5 s)§r: §12×TNT§r entity damage, §cno block damage§r.%n%nThe critical kind is far worse: a §160-tick§r fuse, §150% TNT destruction§r plus §120×TNT damage§r, scattering §14-12§r more with §180-200-tick§r fuses of their own.%n%n§cDo not count your singularities on the floor.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.name=§d§lEntangle the Steam
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.desc=The entangler's output tempo is governed by a saturation function: per cycle, heat §1+= GRADE_COEF × 0.005 × amount/(amount+200,000)§r — feed more and it climbs faster, with diminishing returns.%n%nThree grades, three coefficients: plain §10.5§r, superheated §11.0§r, supercritical §12.0§r. Feed §6200,000 L/s§r and after §1800 cycles = 800 s§r — §61.6 billion L§r in total — one drops; superheated needs only §1400 s§r, supercritical §1200 s§r.%n%nHeat banks at §1100%§r only with a free output bus, then clears.%n%n§3Feed it harder, it works faster.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.name=§d§lThe Entangler, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Steam Singularity Entangler controller (display-only).%n%n§61.6 billion L per singularity§r is an exchange rate worth a dedicated reservoir line; keep the output bus clear, or production simply stops.%n%nSuperheated and supercritical feed halve the cycle, then halve it again — the difference in productivity is night and day.%n%n§2Singularities clock in for shifts now — mass production begins.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.name=§d§lFirst Singularity, Banked
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.desc=The graduation currency's first deposit: dug from the wild or grown in the entangler, provenance is not questioned — one will do.%n%nEvery later bill — hub chips, node bindings, dense pressing, the critical leap — snowballs from this first one.%n%nThe wild route and the factory route converge here; different roads, same vault.%n%n§dHand in one, receive two: the graduation fund lands.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.name=§d§lDense at 1000 to One
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.desc=The Dense State Manipulator presses §11000 units§r into §11§r dense and decompresses back ×1000 — the §3master dispatcher§r of steam grades across the whole chain.%n%nThe fuel bill is modest: §14,000 ticks = 200 s§r per singularity; output factors §1×0.8§r plain, §1×1.0§r critical; fluids always validate before fuel is charged — nothing burns in vain.%n%nTier switches convert the accumulator by GRADE_COEF and keep it — §2changing gears never wipes the ledger§r.%n%n§8§oThe romance of density: a warehouse pressed into a pocket.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.name=§d§lThe Manipulator, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Dense State Manipulator controller (display-only).%n%nIt is the steam ladder's §3elevator§r: press §11000 shares§r into one and save astronomical capacity; decompress upward to feed the machines that want plain grades.%n%nFuel bills settle per unit, and tier switches keep the accumulation — tinker as you please, nothing is lost.%n%n§2One-thousand-to-one, industrialized at last.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.name=§d§lThe Critical Compressor
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.desc=The CSC eats §ddense variants only§r, half-point at §15,000§r: each cycle swallows §15,000 L dense§r, and after §1800 cycles = 800 s§r — §14 million L dense§r in total, §14 billion L§r plain-equivalent — one §dcritical singularity§r finally drops.%n%nThis is chapter E's peak steam bill: plain steam first pressed a thousand-fold by the DSM, then pressed critical here.%n%n§3Critical is a whole steam age pressed into a point.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.name=§d§lCritical Singularity Get
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Critical Steam Compressor controller and one §dcritical singularity§r (display-only).%n%nThe critical kind is the chain's §dpeak currency§r: the drill hub, the mega turbines and the aggregator all name it for their top tiers — you can never hold too many.%n%nIf one lies unclaimed past its §160-tick§r fuse, reread the explosion clauses two quests up.%n%n§8§oHold it steady. Don't shake.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.name=§d§lThe Singularity Drill Hub
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.desc=The SDH is the singularity era's first working machine, and its bill is the plainest: a base diet of §68,000 L/s superheated§r with §cno speedup at all§r — here superheated is only the ticket in, never the throttle.%n%nEach active node bills on top: drilling §62,000/6,000/12,000/20,000§r, mining from §65,000§r all the way to §6240,000 L/s§r; mining radius §132→144 blocks§r, fortune §16-10§r, cycle §180→10 ticks§r.%n%nDrilling draw factors run §110/12/15/18§r over §11×1→8×8 chunks§r; every binding costs §d1 singularity§r — the more you bind, the bigger the appetite.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.name=§d§lDrill Hub, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Singularity Drill Hub plus its drilling and mining nodes (display-only).%n%nThe §68,000 L/s§r superheated base appetite scales linearly with node count — settle the quota with your compressor and reservoirs first.%n%nUpgraded nodes burn §dsingularities§r for fortune and radius; the mine spreads wilder and wilder, the output snowballs.%n%n§2A singularity-driven mine never sleeps.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.name=§3§lEndgame Conveniences
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.desc=The last chapter is all “should have had this sooner” heavyweights: §3the Kinetic Processing Array, the mega turbine array, the Crust Matter Aggregator and machine clusters§r.%n%nThey still drink steam — only the scale leaves the chart, and the supporting reservoirs and mains must grow with them.%n%nMatrix graduates may jump straight here from chapter C, skipping D and E entirely.%n%n§8§oConvenience is technology's final form.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.name=§3§lThe Kinetic Array
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.desc=The endgame's core virtue is steam thrift, and the KPA turns it into an art; it also takes §csuperheated steam only§r — plain steam need not apply. Energy discount base §10.6§r, gear tier 2 presses it to §10.4§r; pipe tiers scale duration §1×0.5/×0.4/×1/3§r; parallelism = §1(1+2×tier)+stacks§r — every liter saved is pure profit.%n%nThe steam-rate ladder falls steeply with voltage: ULV §68.0§r → EV §60.5§r, IV §60.25§r, LuV §60.1§r — the higher the tier, the thriftier.%n%n§3One KPA replaces a machine hall.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.name=§3§lKPA, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Kinetic Processing Array controller (display-only).%n%nThe §10.4 discount§r stacked with §1stacked parallelism§r makes it the central kitchen of endgame recipes; a fed §6superheated main§r is the only prerequisite.%n%nGear and pipe tiers switch freely to match each recipe's tempo — one line runs the whole book.%n%n§2With enough steam it beats a whole machine hall for peace of mind.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.name=§3§lThe Mega Turbine Array
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.desc=The MSTA burns steam back into EU — the pack's only true power plant. Efficiency caps by grade: plain §1150%§r, dense §1200%§r, supercritical §1250%§r, dense supercritical §1300%§r.%n%nSupply priority is written in stone: §3dense supercritical > supercritical > dense superheated > dense > superheated > plain§r; dense and supercritical further demand a §1tier-6§r hull.%n%n§cThe explosion clause is equally stone-written: total dynamo output below the demanded EU, and it blows on the spot.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.name=§3§lCycle Overlimit
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.desc=The Cycle Overlimit Chip is the turbine's §doverdrive switch§r: with all 4 dynamo groups stacked, it keeps raising the output multiplier, EU/L scaling with it — while steam consumption §2stays put§r.%n%nOne chip rewrites “enough” into “overload” — a free slice of power.%n%nCheck your dynamo headroom before fitting it; don't overdraft the safety margin along with the output.%n%n§8§oAn engineer's romance is running past nameplate.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.name=§3§lMSTA, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Mega Steam Turbine Array controller (display-only) — settle your safety margins first; the worked example is the template.%n%nA worked example for the margin math: an §1HV hull§r at power §110§r on single-group superheated at §1100%§r efficiency outputs §1512×10 = 5,120 EU/t§r, drinking §64,096 L/t = 81,920 L/s§r; with this arithmetic done, dynamo sizing becomes a formula.%n%n§cOnly 4×HV dynamo banks (2048 < 5120) detonates on the spot — fit 8A before ignition, safety first.§r%n%n§8§oArithmetic is safety; mental math saves lives.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.name=§3§lCrust Matter, Aggregated
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.desc=The aggregator's bill looks dense but is only three layers of multiplication; the CMA aggregates crust matter on demand: base cost §624,000 L/s§r on the plain tier, or §6240 L/s§r on the dense tier — nearly a thousand-fold apart.%n%nThe steam multiplier is a three-layer product: §1(1+mode+fortune)×(1+0.2×(dim slots−1))×(1+filter cost/100)§r; the targeted multiplier is §1+2500% ÷ the lowest-three weight sum§r.%n%nFortune caps climb with currency: §17§r bare, §111§r with a singularity, §115§r with a critical one — three currencies, three fortune caps.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.name=§3§lCMA, Accepted
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.desc=Acceptance: hand in the Crust Matter Aggregator controller (display-only); the dense tier's ticket is startlingly cheap, the output anything but.%n%nThe dense tier's §6240 L/s§r entry fee buys a §1weight-targeted§r mineral buffet; dimension slots and filters stack the multiplier ever higher.%n%nA critical singularity tops fortune at §115§r — target-filter whatever you lack.%n%n§2The crust is the warehouse; the filter is the pick list.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.name=§3§lClusters and Ten Chain Steps
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.desc=The cluster is GTSR's final form and the steam ledger's final exam; its bill grows exponentially: chain steam = §68,000×1.5^(length−1)§r, §1max 16 steps§r per chain; fixed steam = §68,000×tier multipliers {1,4,16,48}§r.%n%nOperations: preheat §130 s§r; idle decay §11%/s§r, starvation §10.5%/s§r; lubricant and logistics units cost §120→1000§r by tier — starvation hurts more than shutdown, so keep the feed steady.%n%nThe §1ten chain steps§r run from CRUSH §1480 ticks§r to FURNACE §1160 ticks§r; a worked §15-step chain = 40,500+8,000+20 L/s§r.%n%n§8§oThis is not a factory. It is a pipe organ that breathes.§r
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPw.name=§3§lThe Cluster, Accepted
